{"id":"n5_u03_l1","unit_id":"n5_u03","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Combined sounds I: ゃ ゅ ょ","goal":"Read kana pairs such as きゃ and しゅ as one beat each.","introduces":{"kana":["ka_h_kya","ka_h_kyu","ka_h_kyo","ka_h_sha","ka_h_shu","ka_h_sho","ka_h_cha","ka_h_chu","ka_h_cho","ka_h_nya","ka_h_nyu","ka_h_nyo"],"vocab":["v_ocha","v_shashin","v_kyaku","v_shumi","v_konnyaku","v_shokuji"]},"explain":[{"heading":"A small kana changes the vowel","body":["A small ゃ, ゅ or ょ after an い-column kana joins with it into a single beat: き + ゃ = きゃ (kya), し + ゅ = しゅ (shu), ち + ょ = ちょ (cho).","Notice the small size: ゃ (ya) is much smaller than や. Compare きゃ (kya, one beat) with きや (ki-ya, two beats)."],"examples":[{"ja":"おちゃ","reading":"ocha","en":"tea"},{"ja":"しゃしん","reading":"shashin","en":"photo"},{"ja":"こんにゃく","reading":"konnyaku","en":"konjac"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u03_kr01","q_n5u03_kr02","q_n5u03_kr03","q_n5u03_kr04","q_n5u03_mt01","q_n5u03_mt02","q_n5u03_rc01","q_n5u03_rc02","q_n5u03_rc03","q_n5u03_rc04","q_n5u03_vm_ocha","q_n5u03_vm_shashin","q_n5u03_vm_kyaku","q_n5u03_vm_shumi","q_n5u03_vm_konnyaku","q_n5u03_vm_shokuji"],"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_kya","ka_h_kyu","ka_h_kyo","ka_h_sha","ka_h_shu","ka_h_sho","ka_h_cha","ka_h_chu","ka_h_cho","ka_h_nya","ka_h_nyu","ka_h_nyo"],"n":6},{"type":"kana_listen","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_kya","ka_h_kyu","ka_h_kyo","ka_h_sha","ka_h_shu","ka_h_sho","ka_h_cha","ka_h_chu","ka_h_cho","ka_h_nya","ka_h_nyu","ka_h_nyo"],"n":4}]},"exit_check":{"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_kya","ka_h_kyu","ka_h_kyo","ka_h_sha","ka_h_shu","ka_h_sho","ka_h_cha","ka_h_chu","ka_h_cho","ka_h_nya","ka_h_nyu","ka_h_nyo"],"n":6},{"type":"vocab_meaning","from":"vocab","ids":["v_ocha","v_shashin","v_kyaku","v_shumi","v_konnyaku","v_shokuji"],"n":4}],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u03_l2","unit_id":"n5_u03","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Combined sounds II","goal":"Finish the combined sounds across the h, m, r, g, j, b and p rows.","introduces":{"kana":["ka_h_hya","ka_h_hyu","ka_h_hyo","ka_h_mya","ka_h_myu","ka_h_myo","ka_h_rya","ka_h_ryu","ka_h_ryo","ka_h_gya","ka_h_gyu","ka_h_gyo","ka_h_ja","ka_h_ju","ka_h_jo","ka_h_bya","ka_h_byu","ka_h_byo","ka_h_pya","ka_h_pyu","ka_h_pyo"],"vocab":["v_hyaku","v_ryokan","v_jaa"]},"explain":[{"heading":"The same idea in more rows","body":["The pattern repeats: ひゃ hya, みゅ myu, りょ ryo, ぎゃ gya, びゅ byu, ぴょ pyo. じゃ じゅ じょ read \"ja, ju, jo\" (not \"jya\").","Voiced marks stay on the big kana: ぎ + ゃ = ぎゃ, び + ゅ = びゅ, ぴ + ょ = ぴょ."],"examples":[{"ja":"ひゃく","reading":"hyaku","en":"one hundred"},{"ja":"りょかん","reading":"ryokan","en":"Japanese inn"},{"ja":"じゃあ","reading":"jaa","en":"well then"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u03_kr05","q_n5u03_kr06","q_n5u03_kr07","q_n5u03_kr08","q_n5u03_kr09","q_n5u03_kr10","q_n5u03_kr11","q_n5u03_kr12","q_n5u03_mt03","q_n5u03_mt04","q_n5u03_rc05","q_n5u03_rc06","q_n5u03_rc07","q_n5u03_rc08","q_n5u03_rc09","q_n5u03_rc10","q_n5u03_rc11","q_n5u03_rc12","q_n5u03_ty03","q_n5u03_dc02","q_n5u03_vm_hyaku","q_n5u03_vm_ryokan","q_n5u03_vm_jaa"],"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_hya","ka_h_hyu","ka_h_hyo","ka_h_mya","ka_h_myu","ka_h_myo","ka_h_rya","ka_h_ryu","ka_h_ryo","ka_h_gya","ka_h_gyu","ka_h_gyo","ka_h_ja","ka_h_ju","ka_h_jo","ka_h_bya","ka_h_byu","ka_h_byo","ka_h_pya","ka_h_pyu","ka_h_pyo"],"n":6},{"type":"kana_recall","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_hya","ka_h_hyu","ka_h_hyo","ka_h_mya","ka_h_myu","ka_h_myo","ka_h_rya","ka_h_ryu","ka_h_ryo","ka_h_gya","ka_h_gyu","ka_h_gyo","ka_h_ja","ka_h_ju","ka_h_jo","ka_h_bya","ka_h_byu","ka_h_byo","ka_h_pya","ka_h_pyu","ka_h_pyo"],"n":4}]},"exit_check":{"gen":[{"type":"kana_recog","from":"kana","ids":["ka_h_kya","ka_h_kyu","ka_h_kyo","ka_h_sha","ka_h_shu","ka_h_sho","ka_h_cha","ka_h_chu","ka_h_cho","ka_h_nya","ka_h_nyu","ka_h_nyo","ka_h_hya","ka_h_hyu","ka_h_hyo","ka_h_mya","ka_h_myu","ka_h_myo","ka_h_rya","ka_h_ryu","ka_h_ryo","ka_h_gya","ka_h_gyu","ka_h_gyo","ka_h_ja","ka_h_ju","ka_h_jo","ka_h_bya","ka_h_byu","ka_h_byo","ka_h_pya","ka_h_pyu","ka_h_pyo"],"n":6},{"type":"vocab_meaning","from":"vocab","ids":["v_hyaku","v_ryokan","v_jaa"],"n":3}],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u03_l3","unit_id":"n5_u03","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Small っ and long vowels","goal":"Hear and write the pause of っ and the extra beat of a long vowel.","introduces":{"kana":["ka_h_sokuon"],"vocab":["v_gakkou","v_kitte","v_zasshi","v_nikki","v_chotto","v_toukyou","v_kyou","v_ojiisan","v_obaasan","v_yuumei","v_byouin","v_ryouri","v_gyuunyuu","v_hokkaidou","v_oosaka"]},"explain":[{"heading":"Small っ: a pause","body":["A small っ before a consonant makes a short silent beat, and the next consonant is doubled in romaji: がっこう (gakkou), きって (kitte), ざっし (zasshi).","Compare おと (oto, sound) with おっと (otto, husband): the pause changes the word."],"examples":[{"ja":"がっこう","reading":"gakkou","en":"school"},{"ja":"きって","reading":"kitte","en":"stamp"},{"ja":"ちょっと","reading":"chotto","en":"a little"}]},{"heading":"Long vowels","body":["A long vowel lasts two beats. In hiragana it is written with an extra vowel kana: ああ, いい, うう, ええ (ei), おお or おう (ou).","The length changes meaning: おばあさん (grandmother) versus おばさん (aunt); おじいさん (grandfather) versus おじさん (uncle)."],"examples":[{"ja":"おばあさん","reading":"obaasan","en":"grandmother"},{"ja":"とうきょう","reading":"toukyou","en":"Tokyo"},{"ja":"おおさか","reading":"oosaka","en":"Osaka"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u03_mo01","q_n5u03_mo02","q_n5u03_mo03","q_n5u03_mo04","q_n5u03_mo05","q_n5u03_mo06","q_n5u03_mo07","q_n5u03_mo08","q_n5u03_ro01","q_n5u03_ro02","q_n5u03_ro03","q_n5u03_ro04","q_n5u03_dc03","q_n5u03_dc04","q_n5u03_dc05","q_n5u03_ty04","q_n5u03_ty05","q_n5u03_vm_gakkou","q_n5u03_vm_kitte","q_n5u03_vm_zasshi","q_n5u03_vm_nikki","q_n5u03_vm_chotto","q_n5u03_vm_toukyou","q_n5u03_vm_kyou","q_n5u03_vm_ojiisan","q_n5u03_vm_obaasan","q_n5u03_vm_yuumei","q_n5u03_vm_byouin","q_n5u03_vm_ryouri","q_n5u03_vm_gyuunyuu","q_n5u03_vm_hokkaidou","q_n5u03_vm_oosaka"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n5u03_mo01","q_n5u03_mo04","q_n5u03_mo06","q_n5u03_ro01","q_n5u03_ro03","q_n5u03_ro04","q_n5u03_dc03","q_n5u03_ty06","q_n5u03_ty07","q_n5u03_ty08"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u03_l4","unit_id":"n5_u03","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Saying what something is: X は Y です","goal":"Make your first full sentences.","introduces":{"vocab":["v_desu","v_san","v_gakusei","v_kaishain","v_nihonjin","v_dare","v_namae"],"grammar":["g_wa_desu"]},"explain":[{"heading":"Topic + は + description + です","body":["わたし は がくせい です means \"I am a student\". は marks the topic and is pronounced \"wa\". です ends the sentence politely.","Add さん after someone else's name: たなか さん. Never add it to your own name."],"examples":[{"ja":"わたし は がくせい です","reading":"watashi wa gakusei desu","en":"I am a student."},{"ja":"たなか さん は せんせい です","reading":"tanaka san wa sensei desu","en":"Ms. Tanaka is a teacher."}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u03_gw01","q_n5u03_gw02","q_n5u03_gw03","q_n5u03_gw04","q_n5u03_gw05","q_n5u03_tr01","q_n5u03_tr02","q_n5u03_tr03","q_n5u03_tr04","q_n5u03_vm_desu","q_n5u03_vm_san","q_n5u03_vm_gakusei","q_n5u03_vm_kaishain","q_n5u03_vm_nihonjin","q_n5u03_vm_dare","q_n5u03_vm_namae"]},"context":{"question_ids":["q_n5u03_gw06","q_n5u03_gw07","q_n5u03_gw08","q_n5u03_tr05","q_n5u03_tr06","q_n5u03_ty09","q_n5u03_ty10"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n5u03_gw01","q_n5u03_gw03","q_n5u03_gw04","q_n5u03_gw05","q_n5u03_gw07","q_n5u03_tr01","q_n5u03_tr03"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u03_l5","unit_id":"n5_u03","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Asking questions: ですか","goal":"Ask and answer simple questions and introduce yourself.","introduces":{"vocab":["v_donata","v_onamae","v_kochira","v_nan"],"grammar":["g_ka_question"]},"explain":[{"heading":"か makes a question","body":["Put か at the end: あなた は がくせい です か = \"Are you a student?\". The word order stays the same.","Answer with はい or いいえ, then the statement: はい わたし は がくせい です."],"examples":[{"ja":"あなた は がくせい です か","reading":"anata wa gakusei desu ka","en":"Are you a student?"},{"ja":"おなまえ は なん です か","reading":"onamae wa nan desu ka","en":"What is your name?"}]},{"heading":"Introducing yourself","body":["はじめまして, then your name with です, then よろしく おねがいします. The other person replies こちら こそ."],"examples":[{"ja":"はじめまして たなか です","reading":"hajimemashite tanaka desu","en":"Nice to meet you. I'm Tanaka."}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u03_gk01","q_n5u03_gk02","q_n5u03_gk03","q_n5u03_gk04","q_n5u03_gk05","q_n5u03_dg03","q_n5u03_dg04","q_n5u03_tr07","q_n5u03_tr08","q_n5u03_vm_donata","q_n5u03_vm_onamae","q_n5u03_vm_kochira","q_n5u03_vm_nan"]},"context":{"question_ids":["q_n5u03_gk06","q_n5u03_gk07","q_n5u03_gk08","q_n5u03_dg01","q_n5u03_dg02","q_n5u03_dg05","q_n5u03_dg06","q_n5u03_tr09","q_n5u03_tr10"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n5u03_gk01","q_n5u03_gk02","q_n5u03_gk04","q_n5u03_gk05","q_n5u03_gk06","q_n5u03_dg03","q_n5u03_dg06"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u03_l6","unit_id":"n5_u03","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Listen and read","goal":"Hear long vowels and small kana, and read a name card and an introduction.","introduces":{},"explain":[{"heading":"Length matters","body":["In Japanese, a short pause or a long vowel changes the word. Listen carefully for the number of beats."],"examples":[{"ja":"おじいさん","reading":"ojiisan","en":"grandfather"},{"ja":"おじさん","reading":"ojisan","en":"uncle"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u03_gl01","q_n5u03_gl02","q_n5u03_gl03","q_n5u03_gl04","q_n5u03_gl05","q_n5u03_gl06","q_n5u03_gl07","q_n5u03_gl08","q_n5u03_dc01"]},"context":{"question_ids":["q_n5u03_rq01","q_n5u03_rq02","q_n5u03_rq03","q_n5u03_rq04","q_n5u03_rq05"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n5u03_gl03","q_n5u03_gl05","q_n5u03_gl06","q_n5u03_gl07","q_n5u03_rq01","q_n5u03_rq04","q_n5u03_dc01"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u03_l7","unit_id":"n5_u03","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Putting words together","goal":"Mix the new sounds and sentence patterns with what you learned in units 1 and 2.","introduces":{},"explain":[{"heading":"Review through use","body":["Tell people who you are, ask who they are, and name things around you. Words from the first two units keep coming back so they stay fresh."],"examples":[{"ja":"しゅみ は しゃしん です","reading":"shumi wa shashin desu","en":"My hobby is photography."},{"ja":"おちゃ は おいしい です","reading":"ocha wa oishii desu","en":"Tea is delicious."}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u03_tr11","q_n5u03_tr12","q_n5u03_tr13","q_n5u03_tr14","q_n5u03_ty01","q_n5u03_ty02","q_n5u03_sr_ao","q_n5u03_sr_aki","q_n5u03_sr_kao","q_n5u03_sr_asa","q_n5u03_sr_ushi","q_n5u03_sr_sushi","q_n5u03_sr_oishii","q_n5u03_sr_tako","q_n5u03_sr_chiisai","q_n5u03_sr_ichi","q_n5u03_sr_niku","q_n5u03_sr_anata","q_n5u03_sr_fune","q_n5u03_sr_mochi","q_n5u03_sr_okane","q_n5u03_sr_sakura","q_n5u03_sr_nihon","q_n5u03_sr_haru"]},"context":{"question_ids":["q_n5u03_sr_yume","q_n5u03_sr_gohan","q_n5u03_sr_tomodachi","q_n5u03_sr_mizu","q_n5u03_sr_kodomo","q_n5u03_sr_boushi","q_n5u03_sr_budou"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n5u03_tr11","q_n5u03_tr13","q_n5u03_tr14","q_n5u03_gw01","q_n5u03_gk02","q_n5u03_sr_ao","q_n5u03_sr_aki","q_n5u03_sr_kao"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"}
